From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:31:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a restart carries background subagents to their
 boundaries and stops no other thread

An agent kept the ident of the thread that ran its last turn after the turn ended, and thread idents are reused at once (a new thread gets the ident of the last one that ended; gateway turn threads are pooled). A background subagent stopped for a restart handoff (delegation.restart_handoff) while it waited on its processes or helpers aimed its interrupt at that ident, so whatever ran there next was interrupted: another chat's foreground device command ended with "[Command interrupted]" (exit 130) at the old gateway's SIGTERM while the per-turn carry (gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn) was meant to run it to its end. run_conversation now unbinds the execution thread when its outermost call returns; a stop between turns still reaches the next turn through _interrupt_requested.

The per-turn carry also stopped every background subagent at the release (restart_handoff_grace_seconds), cutting its model call, which the next gateway then made again. The carrier now carries them like the turns: each subagent in a turn runs its model call and tool round to their end and stops at the top of its next iteration (turn_boundary_handoff.request(tool_round=False)), its state recorded from its own cleanup; one not in a turn stops at once, and one that has not reached a boundary by the carry ceiling less 60 s is yielded and stopped as before. The release does not wait for them; the carrier keeps its background processes and writes turn_carry.processes_handed (which has the next gateway adopt them) only once they stopped, and a unit whose children all finished meanwhile is still handed over, so the next gateway, which owns the chats, delivers it. A unit the carry hands off is not stopped again by the stop that follows.
